## 4. How much is fusion worth?

### 4.1 Method

We selected corpora spanning the modality combinations the field uses: conversational
text–audio–video (MELD), speech with peripheral physiology (KEMDy20), EEG with eye
movements (SEED, SEED-IV), and EEG with peripheral physiology (AMIGOS, DEAP). For each
we located a paper reporting unimodal ablations alongside the fused system, obtained
the PDF, and read the cells from the table. Numbers obtained from search summaries were
discarded and re-read; three of them were wrong, one by three points (Section 4.3).

Two corpora resisted that procedure. CMU-MOSI and CMU-MOSEI dominate the
missing-modality literature, but no source table pairing unimodal with fused rows under
one architecture was reachable to us, and after three second-hand entries had turned out
wrong we were not willing to record remembered numbers. Section 4.4 measures those two
directly instead.

