and its test majority is positive, so a constant predictor that can only see the
training split scores 37.90 while the best constant predictor scores 62.10 — the same
formula, 24 points apart, depending on which $\pi_0$ is used. Finally, every constant
predictor on both corpora scores $\kappa = 0.000$ exactly, which is Proposition 4 of
Section 5.3 confirmed on real data rather than on sampled confusion matrices.

